## Common Borrow Errors and Fixes

### Error 1: Use After Move

```xiom
// BAD:
let v = Vec[Int].new();
let v2 = v;
v.push(1);  // ERROR: v was moved!

// FIX: Clone if you need both
let v = Vec[Int].new();
let v2 = v.clone();
v.push(1);
v2.push(2);
```

### Error 2: Cannot Borrow as Mutable and Immutable

```xiom
// BAD:
var data = Vec[Int].new();
data.push(1);
let r = &data;
let w = &mut data;  // ERROR: & already exists!

// FIX: End the read borrow first with a scope
var data = Vec[Int].new();
data.push(1);
{ let r = &data; io.println(r.len()); }
let w = &mut data;  // OK: r is dead
```

### Error 3: Cannot Return Reference to Local

```xiom
// BAD:
fn bad() -> &Vec[Int] {
  let v = Vec[Int].new();
  return &v;  // ERROR: v is destroyed on return!
}

// FIX: Return the owned value
fn good() -> Vec[Int] {
  let v = Vec[Int].new();
  return v;  // OK: ownership moves to caller
}
```

### Error 4: Move While Borrowed

```xiom
// BAD:
let v = Vec[Int].new();
let r = &v;
let v2 = v;  // ERROR: can't move v while borrowed!

// FIX: End the borrow first
let v = Vec[Int].new();
{ let r = &v; io.println(r.len()); }
let v2 = v;  // OK
```

